course: dictionary
lesson: 60
title: Ache: a dull pain that lasts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ache can be a noun (an ache) or a verb (to ache). An ache is a pain that goes on for a long time but is not sharp. «Noah's dad got him a proper chair, and his back stopped aching.» Aching here means the back hurt with a dull, steady pain, and the chair made it stop.
explain: Names for aches tell you where the pain is: headache, toothache, stomach ache, earache and backache. «Anxiety can cause headaches, tummy aches and trouble sleeping.» Aches is the plural, so it means more than one ache.
explain: Ache can also mean wanting something very much. Stories use it for feelings too, so a heart can ache with sadness. When you meet ache, ask: is this a body pain, or a strong feeling? The words around it will tell you.
fact: Ache (noun) means a pain that goes on for a long time but is not sharp.
fact: Ache (verb) means to hurt with a dull, steady pain.
fact: Common aches include headache, toothache, stomach ache, earache and backache.
fact: «Aches and pains» is a phrase for many small hurts all over the body.
fact: If an ache lasts a long time, tell an adult or a doctor.
exercise: «Noah's dad got him a proper chair, and his back stopped aching.» What does aching mean here? | A loud noise | A sharp, sudden cut | *A dull, steady pain
exercise: Which name is for a pain in your ears? | *Earache | Toothache | Headache
exercise: Which word is the plural of ache, as in «tummy aches»? | ached | aching | *aches
test: The phrase «aches and pains» means: | a sudden loud bang | *many small aches and pains | a happy song
test: To ache for something means to: | *want it very much | hurt with a sharp, sudden pain | forget it quickly
exam: Which is the best meaning of ache in «Her heart ached for her lost puppy»? | Hurt with a sharp cut | Grew very tall | *Felt a sad longing, wanting her puppy back very much | Was loud and noisy
